translated_text:
Article 17
(1) Implementation of protection for female workers/laborers to provide protection from acts of economic exploitation and cruel, inhumane treatment and to ensure proper appreciation for their work. (2) Female workers/laborers as referred to in paragraph (1) shall receive protection for:
a. Recognition of rights, wages and decent working conditions; b. Health insurance and social security for employment; c. Access to information and legal consultation services; d. Opportunities to obtain knowledge and skills to improve status;

